<section class="section prose container">
  <h2>1. General</h2>
  <p>This privacy policy applies to the use of the website of Ofir Omer, Adv. (the "Site") and explains what data is collected in connection with using the Site, how it is used, and how to reach out with any questions regarding privacy.</p>

  <h2>2. Consent and Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>Continued use of the Site constitutes agreement to the terms of this privacy policy. The firm may update this policy from time to time; the updated version will be published on this page, with the date of the last update noted at the bottom of the page.</p>

  <h2>3. Information You Provide</h2>
  <p>When you reach out via the Site's contact form, the firm receives the details entered in the form (full name, phone, email, subject, and message). As of the date this policy was last updated, the contact form opens the user's own email client and sends the inquiry directly to the firm's email address — the data is not stored on the Site's server.</p>

  <h2>4. Automatically Collected Information</h2>
  <p>The Site is hosted on GitHub Pages and uses fonts served from Google Fonts servers. The Contact page embeds a Google Maps view to show the office location. These services may, as part of their routine operation, log basic technical access data (such as IP address and browser type), and the maps service may set its own cookies in accordance with Google's privacy policy. As of the date this policy was last updated, the Site itself does not use analytics tools (such as Google Analytics) and does not use cookies of its own for tracking or advertising purposes. Should this change in the future, this policy will be updated accordingly.</p>

  <h2>5. Browser Display Preferences</h2>
  <p>The Site stores display preferences only, locally in the user's browser (localStorage) — such as light/dark mode and accessibility settings (font size, contrast, link underlining, reduced motion). This information is stored solely on the user's device, is never transmitted to any server, and is not used to identify the user.</p>

  <h2>6. Sharing Information with Third Parties</h2>
  <p>The firm does not sell or rent personal information to third parties. Information may be exposed to technical service providers that support the Site's operation (such as the GitHub Pages hosting service, the Google Fonts service, and the Google Maps service), and in any case required by law.</p>

  <h2>7. Data Security</h2>
  <p>The firm takes reasonable measures to protect information handled in connection with the Site, but cannot guarantee absolute protection against unauthorized access.</p>

  <h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>The Site is not intended for use by minors under the age of 18 and is not designed to knowingly collect information about them.</p>

  <h2>9. Your Rights</h2>
  <p>Under the Israeli Privacy Protection Law, 5741-1981, any individual who has provided their details is entitled to request access to the information provided about them, and to request its correction or deletion, subject to applicable law.</p>

  <h2>10. Contact for Privacy Inquiries</h2>
  <p>For any question regarding this privacy policy, please reach out via the phone number or email address listed on the <a href="{{ '/en/contact/' | url }}">Contact</a> page.</p>

  <p>Last updated: {{ site.privacy.lastUpdated }}</p>
